Sully (also known as Sully: Miracle on the Hudson) is a 2016 American biographical drama film directed by Clint Eastwood and written
by Todd Komarnicki, based on the 2009 autobiography Highest Duty by Chesley "Sully" Sullenberger and Jeffrey Zaslow.

12
01:00:37,894 --> 01:00:43,894
Tom Hanks stars as Sullenberger, with Aaron Eckhart as Jeffrey Skiles, and co-stars
Laura Linney, Anna Gunn, Autumn Reeser, Holt McCallany, and Jamey Sheridan.

13
01:05:41,052 --> 01:05:47,052
The film follows Sullenberger's 2009 emergency landing of US Airways Flight 1549 on the Hudson River, in
which all 155 passengers and crew survived, and the subsequent publicity and investigation.

14
01:10:44,210 --> 01:10:50,210
Sully premiered at the 43rd Telluride Film Festival on September 2,
2016, and was released in the United States by Warner Bros.

15
01:15:47,368 --> 01:15:53,368
on September 9, 2016, in conventional and IMAX theaters.

16
01:20:50,526 --> 01:20:56,526
The film received generally positive reviews from critics and grossed over $240 million worldwide, but created controversy with its fictionalized portrayal of the National Transportation Safety Board (NTSB) as "prosecutorial and
closed-minded." The American Film Institute and National Board of Review each selected it as one of their ten best films of 2016, and it was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Sound Editing at the 89th Academy Awards.

